OL,3,GNEWSACookery classes help Afghan pupil
OL,4,A'feel at home'
OL,5,
OL,6,F"It was good to see other people trying
OL,7,Fyour food - I was looking at every side
OL,8,Fand everyone was eating it, finishing
OL,9,Fall the food, I loved it."
OL,11,FNine-year-old Arsalan is one of 18
OL,12,FAfghan refugees at Albrighton Primary
OL,13,FSchool, in Shropshire, where pupils
OL,14,Fhave been bonding and learning about
OL,15,Feach other's cultures through food.
OL,17,FEach Tuesday, a small group of pupils
OL,18,Fhave worked with a chef from Shrewsbury
OL,19,FFood Hub to turn surplus food into a
OL,20,Ftraditional Afghan dish, and later
OL,21,Fhosting a meal for families in their
OL,22,Fschool hall.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
